can you explain to me what the composite pattern do, when we use it, and what th problem dose it fix ?
------------AI Response-------------
What the Composite Pattern Does
The Composite pattern lets you compose objects into tree structures to represent part-whole hierarchies. It enables client code to treat individual objects and complex groups of objects uniformly.
As demonstrated in the provided code structure:
⚬	An abstract component (HtmlTag) defines a unified interface for all objects in the tree.
⚬	Leaf objects (HtmlElement) represent individual end nodes that perform operations directly.
⚬	Composite objects (HtmlParentElement) represent groups or branches that contain a list of child components, allowing operations to cascade recursively through the entire tree.
The Problem It Fixes
It fixes the complexity and tight coupling that occur when client code has to distinguish between single objects and container objects. Without this pattern, your code would require messy conditional checks (such as instanceof checks) to figure out whether it is dealing with a single item or a container before executing an operation.
When to Use It
⚬	When you need to represent part-whole hierarchies of objects in a tree structure.
⚬	When you want client code to ignore the differences between composite structures and individual objects, allowing them to interact with both through the exact same interface.

